 "description": "Valero2006_Adenine_TernaryCycle\nBioModels BIOMD0000000231 (curated). SBML file: BIOMD0000000231_url.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 100000 time units (SED-ML: BIOMD0000000231_url.sedml (auto-generated placeholder); duration chosen from the dynamics: still changing at cap), sampling 100.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 3.62e-06 of species peak (worst: AMP)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] 'NADH' goes below zero in the SBML: integrated as NADH_o = value + 20000, output as NADH = OUTC[NADH_o;-20000*source]\n  [info] v1: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] v2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] v3: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed",
